          "id": "tree-w3c-keyboard-pattern",
          "priority": "P1",
          "title": "Missing W3C tree keyboard interaction pattern",
          "description": "Tree component has basic ARIA roles (role='tree', role='treeitem', aria-expanded) but lacks W3C-recommended keyboard navigation. W3C ARIA Authoring Practices requires arrow-key navigation for managed-focus trees. Current implementation only supports Tab-based focus. Does not implement either (a) roving tabindex with arrow-key handlers or (b) managed focus with aria-activedescendant.",
          "actualBehavior": "Only Tab key moves focus between tree items. ArrowRight/ArrowLeft have no effect. Users cannot expand/collapse nodes or navigate efficiently via keyboard.",
          "expectedBehavior": "Implement W3C tree keyboard interaction (https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/treeview/): ArrowRight expands focused node (if collapsed), ArrowLeft collapses it (if expanded). Up/Down arrow keys move focus to previous/next visible item. Use either roving tabindex or managed focus pattern.",
          "userImpact": "Keyboard-only and screen reader users cannot efficiently navigate tree hierarchies. Violates WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard Accessibility).",
          "verificationMethod": "Code inspection of keyboard event handlers; testing with keyboard and screen reader; W3C ARIA tree pattern specification verification",
          "verificationConfidence": "Code-reviewed",
          "wcagCriteria": ["2.1.1 Keyboard"]
        }
      ],
      "decision": "Improve",
      "reasoning": "Tree component has basic ARIA roles (tree, treeitem, aria-expanded) but is missing W3C compliant keyboard navigation pattern and aria-activedescendant. Requires implementation of arrow key handlers and focus management."
